PS-005 — Replace destructive database fallback

Affected file: "AppDatabase.kt"

Current concern

The reviewed Room database configuration uses "fallbackToDestructiveMigration(true)". When Room cannot find a suitable migration, destructive fallback can delete and recreate database tables, causing data loss.

Required changes

1. Remove destructive migration fallback from production configuration.
2. Document the current database schema and version.
3. Add explicit Room migrations from each supported released version.
4. Use schema export and commit schema snapshots to version control.
5. Test upgrades from existing versions using representative databases.
6. Preserve scan history and user preferences when upgrading.
7. Define a deliberate recovery strategy for genuinely unrecoverable database states.
8. If data reset is ever used for development, ensure it is confined to debug-only builds.

Required tests

- Upgrade from every supported database version.
- Existing scan records survive migration.
- Existing preferences survive migration.
- Newly added columns receive valid migration defaults.
- Interrupted or failed migration is handled safely.
- Fresh installation creates the expected schema.

Acceptance criterion: Supported upgrades do not silently erase user data.

