10. Final Engineering Recommendation

Do not begin by rewriting the whole application or adding more AI features. Preserve the existing working architecture where possible and remediate the highest-risk paths in small, reviewable changes.

The recommended order is:

1. Establish the baseline.
2. Eliminate false-safe and synthetic-fallback risks.
3. Secure authentication and Gemini access.
4. Validate evidence and AI output.
5. Protect database integrity and personal information.
6. Expand tests and establish CI.
7. Complete release hardening and controlled testing.

This document is the remediation specification. It is not evidence that the fixes have already been implemented or that PureScan has passed production testing. Each acceptance criterion must be supported by actual code changes and recorded verification results before the corresponding issue is closed.